GO -- a GRADED spiking read-out (a per-slot LIF read, warm-started from the closed-form ridge at a low output gain then BPTT-fine-tuned through the spike nonlinearity; the read is argmax over the OUTPUT LIF neurons' SUMMED SPIKE COUNT) RESOLVES the object-relative structural role on the FROZEN spiking reservoir, GENUINELY ON SPIKES + 6-seed-BLIND. LIKE-FOR-LIKE vs the FIXED SPIKING WTA (the confound the last GO was retracted for -- NOT repeated): objrel-slot0(THEME) 0.50->1.00, recovering on 6/6 (all 3/3 BLIND) at the dev-frozen op-point; canonical NOT regressed (>=0.90 all 6). THE OPERATIVE LEVER is the GRADED (non-saturated) spike-count read: the SATURATION ablation (~10x output gain -> every role max-fires, the sub-1% margin is quantized away) collapses objrel 1.00->0.00 -- the same failure mode as the fixed WTA's Dale-shift + mutual inhibition. HONESTLY REPORTED (not the operative lever): the nonlinear LIF hidden is NOT required (the linear H=0 graded read also recovers objrel, 1.00), and pure random-init BPTT FAILS (0.00) -- the ridge warm-start is load-bearing for TRAINING the fragile minority direction, the graded deployment is load-bearing for the READ. Silencing the output drive collapses the read to chance (#0: the decision is in the output spikes); scrambled targets -> chance (role-specific). NO sim/ edit; CPU/numpy. Scope: the ridge weights are the read-out's learned linear parameters, deployed + read as graded spiking neurons (NOT a host f@Ws argmax) -- a genuinely-spiking deployment surpass of the saturated fixed WTA, distinct from a nonlinear-BPTT surpass (which the evidence does NOT support here).
